# Wiki Schema — Literature Review

## Project description

Sustained inquiry into a research topic via papers, articles, and notes.
Sources are mostly PDFs and arxiv links; output is a wiki of methods,
findings, and an evolving thesis.

## Page conventions

Wiki/concepts pages:
- H1 = canonical concept name (e.g. "Retrieval-Augmented Generation").
- One opening paragraph defining the concept.
- ## Key claims — bulleted, each cited inline with [[raw:<id>]].
- ## Methods (when applicable).
- ## Open questions.

## Page types
- Concept (algorithm, method, theory)
- Paper (single citation, includes Abstract / Method / Result sections)
- Researcher / Author

## Linking conventions

Use the typed edges aggressively:
- `cites` for fact-based claims with explicit source
- `contradicts` only when both sides have explicit citations on the same question
- `supersedes` when a newer method replaces an older one (note the year)
- `elaborates` when this page goes deeper than the linked page

## Ingest guidance

- For survey papers: extract aggressively — 10-20 concept pages is healthy.
- For single-finding papers: 2-4 concept pages is enough.
- For position pieces / opinion articles: usually 1-2 pages + heavy linking to existing concepts.
